{
  "schema": "jdewitt.vocab-conjugate/1",
  "scope": "Bijection on the output vocabulary of a quantized artifact: storage fidelity, the pair table, and the pre/post cosine of every mapped row. No model is loaded, no logits or generations are read, and no behavioural claim is made.",
  "method": "Each pair names a denial opener and a compliance opener. Both surfaces are resolved against the artifact tokenizer in two contexts (bare and with the leading space running text carries) and must be exactly one token in both; the resolved ids are then transposed in the token-row matrix. For a head tied to the token embedding (no output.weight) the transposed matrix is both the embedding and the output head, so the edit also conjugates the input side; the report names it as tied. The write reuses ggufio.edit_tensors: every untouched tensor is copied byte for byte and the edited tensor is requantized at its own stored type, so every tensor offset and byte length stays put and the pre-edit bytes restore the file. Storage fidelity only: no model, no logits, no generation, no behavioral claim, removal_measured false.",
  "gated": "A behavioural claim is out of scope: the rest of the refusal sentence is planned upstream, so an opener-only conjugation is expected to glue a compliant opening to a refusal body. Measuring that needs a serve, which this card forbids.",
  "removal_measured": false,
